  "id": "Compound::DB00116 - Gene::4522",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Tetrahydrofolic Acid (THFA) and Mthfd1, as THFA binds to Mthfd2, which is involved in multiple enzymatic activities related to folate metabolism. These activities include the conversion of methylenetetrahydrofolate to tetrahydrofolate and the hydrolysis of methenyltetrahydrofolate. Mthfd1, which is a participant in these processes, is therefore likely to be a target of THFA. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and robust interaction, suggesting that THFA modulates Mthfd1 through its interaction with Mthfd2, which in turn influences folate metabolism. The overlapping roles of Mthfd2 in different enzymatic pathways further support the idea that THFA acts on a shared regulatory node, Mthfd2, to affect Mthfd1. This mechanism aligns with the known role of THFA in regulating folate metabolism and suggests that THFA may exert its effects through a common pathway involving Mthfd2 and Mthfd1.",
